                    <p class=MsoNormal><span style="font-family:仿宋;mso-bidi-font-family:'Times New Roman';font-size:12.0000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><font face="仿宋"><p style="text-align: justify;"><span style="font-family: 'times new roman', times, serif;">The "<strong>Healthy Aging (H)</strong>" course covers cutting-edge topics such as the molecular basis of aging, characteristics of aging, the relationship between aging and disease, and therapeutic strategies and interventions for aging. The course is rich in content, taught by renowned professors in the field, and through theoretical lectures and case studies, it deepens students' understanding of the aging process and cultivates their ability to explore aging interventions at the molecular level, aiming to train professional talents for the field of aging research in the future.</span></p></font></span><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman';mso-fareast-font-family:仿宋;font-size:10.5000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><o:p></o:p></span></p>
